# ClickHouse SQL Conventions

## Database: `otel`

## Core Tables

| Table | Engine | Purpose |
|-------|--------|---------|
| `otel_traces` | MergeTree | Spans — TraceId, SpanId, SpanName, Duration, SpanAttributes, ResourceAttributes |
| `otel_logs` | MergeTree | Logs — TraceId, Body, SeverityText, LogAttributes, ResourceAttributes |
| `otel_metrics_gauge` | MergeTree | Gauge OTLP metrics — MetricName, Value, TimeUnix, Attributes, ResourceAttributes |
| `otel_metrics_sum` | MergeTree | Sum/counter OTLP metrics — Value, AggregationTemporality, IsMonotonic, exemplars |
| `otel_metrics_summary` | MergeTree | Summary OTLP metrics — Count, Sum, ValueAtQuantiles |
| `otel_metrics_histogram` | MergeTree | Histogram OTLP metrics — buckets, Count, Sum, Min, Max, AggregationTemporality |
| `otel_metrics_exp_histogram` | MergeTree | Exponential histogram OTLP metrics |
| `otel_metrics` | View | Union of all five metric tables — Timestamp, Value, Count, Sum, MetricSource |
| `stack_trace_events` | MergeTree | Symbolicated + grouped stack traces |
| `project_monthly_usage` | AggregatingMergeTree | Monthly aggregates by `project_id`, `month`, `source` |
| `root_cause_cache` | ReplacingMergeTree(`cached_at`) | RCA cache: `ProjectId`, keys, JSON `baseline` / `segments` |

Materialized views `project_monthly_*_mv` populate `project_monthly_usage` from traces, logs, metrics, and stack traces.

Heatmap DDL lives in `backend/db/prod/clickhouse/otel.interaction_heatmaps_daily.sql`:

| Table / object | Engine | Purpose |
|----------------|--------|---------|
| `interaction_heatmaps_daily` | SummingMergeTree | Daily binned aggregates for the heatmap API |
| `interaction_heatmaps_daily_mv` | Materialized view | Aggregates from `otel_logs` where `PulseType = 'app.click'` |

## Key Columns in `otel_traces`

`TraceId`, `SpanId`, `ParentSpanId`, `SpanName`, `SpanKind`, `ServiceName`, `Duration` (nanoseconds), `StatusCode`, `StatusMessage`, `SpanAttributes` (Map), `ResourceAttributes` (Map), `Timestamp` (DateTime64)

## Materialized Columns

These columns are extracted from Map attributes at insert time. **Always use these instead of accessing the Map columns directly** — they are faster and indexed.

| Column | Source Key | Source Map | Available In |
|--------|-----------|------------|--------------|
| `ProjectId` | `project.id` | ResourceAttributes | all tables |
| `PulseType` | `pulse.type` | SpanAttributes/LogAttributes | all tables |
| `SessionId` | `session.id` | SpanAttributes/LogAttributes/Attributes | all tables |
| `AppVersion` | `app.build_name` | ResourceAttributes | all tables |
| `SDKVersion` | `rum.sdk.version` | ResourceAttributes | all tables |
| `Platform` | `os.name` | ResourceAttributes | all tables |
| `OsVersion` | `os.version` | ResourceAttributes | all tables |
| `GeoState` | `geo.region.iso_code` | SpanAttributes/LogAttributes/Attributes | all tables |
| `GeoCountry` | `geo.country.iso_code` | SpanAttributes/LogAttributes/Attributes | all tables |
| `DeviceModel` | `device.model.name` | ResourceAttributes | all tables |
| `NetworkProvider` | `network.carrier.name` | SpanAttributes/LogAttributes/Attributes | all tables |
| `UserId` | `user.id` | `app.installation.id` | SpanAttributes/LogAttributes/Attributes | traces, logs, metrics |
| `MeteringSessionId` | `pulse.metering.session.id` | SpanAttributes/LogAttributes/Attributes | traces, logs, metrics, `stack_trace_events` |
| `WebVitalName` | `web_vital.name` | LogAttributes | `otel_logs` only |
| `WebVitalValue` | `web_vital.value` (as `Float64` via `toFloat64OrZero`) | LogAttributes | `otel_logs` only |
| `WebVitalRating` | `web_vital.rating` | LogAttributes | `otel_logs` only |

`otel_traces` also has a deprecated `SpanType` column (same source as `PulseType`).

## `root_cause_cache`

Columns: `ProjectId`, `interaction_name`, `date`, `window_end_utc`, `mode`, `baseline`, `segments`, `cached_at`. Row-level access uses the same `otel.*` policy as other analytics tables (`ProjectId`).

## `project_monthly_usage`

Underlying column is `project_id` (alias of `ProjectId` in MV SELECTs). Query with time filter on `month` and filter `project_id` / `ProjectId` consistently with your context.

## ORDER BY Keys

All tables start their ORDER BY with `ProjectId` for multi-tenant isolation:

| Table | ORDER BY |
|-------|----------|
| `otel_traces` | `(ProjectId, ServiceName, PulseType, SpanName, Timestamp)` |
| `otel_logs` | `(ProjectId, PulseType, EventName, Timestamp)` (dev + prod DDL in `backend/db/*/clickhouse/01_otel.otel_logs.sql` / `otel.otel_logs.sql`) |
| `otel_metrics_gauge` | `(ProjectId, ServiceName, MetricName, Attributes, toUnixTimestamp64Nano(TimeUnix))` |
| `otel_metrics_sum` | `(ProjectId, ServiceName, MetricName, Attributes, toUnixTimestamp64Nano(TimeUnix))` |
| `otel_metrics_summary` | `(ProjectId, ServiceName, MetricName, Attributes, toUnixTimestamp64Nano(TimeUnix))` |
| `otel_metrics_histogram` | `(ProjectId, ServiceName, MetricName, Attributes, toUnixTimestamp64Nano(TimeUnix))` |
| `otel_metrics_exp_histogram` | `(ProjectId, ServiceName, MetricName, Attributes, toUnixTimestamp64Nano(TimeUnix))` |
| `stack_trace_events` | `(ProjectId, GroupId, ExceptionType, toUnixTimestamp(Timestamp))` |
| `interaction_heatmaps_daily` | `(Date, ProjectId, ScreenName, AppVersion, Platform, GeographicalRegion, Breakpoint, XBin, YBin)` |

## `stack_trace_events` Key Columns

`Timestamp`, `TraceId`, `SpanId`, `GroupId`, `Fingerprint`, `ExceptionType`, `ExceptionMessage`, `ExceptionStackTrace`, `Title`, `ScreenName`, `Interactions`, `Platform`, `AppVersion`, `OsVersion`, `DeviceModel`, `ResourceAttributes`, `LogAttributes`, `ProjectId`, `PulseType`

## Pulse-Specific Span Attributes

Accessed via `SpanAttributes['key']` (for traces) or `LogAttributes['key']` (for logs):
- `pulse.type`, `pulse.interaction.name`, `screen.name`
- `app.build_name` (→ `AppVersion`), `os.name` (→ `Platform`), `device.model.name` (→ `DeviceModel`)
- Web vitals on logs (`pulse.type = 'web_vital'`): prefer **`WebVitalName`**, **`WebVitalValue`**, **`WebVitalRating`**
  over `LogAttributes['web_vital.name'|'web_vital.value'|'web_vital.rating']`

## Multi-Tenant Data Isolation

Each project has dedicated ClickHouse credentials (stored in MySQL `clickhouse_project_credentials` table). During project creation, `ClickhouseProjectService` creates:

1. **ClickHouse user**: `project_{sanitized_project_id}`
2. **Row policy**: One permissive policy on `otel.*`, named `policy_{sanitized_project_id}`, filtering by `ProjectId` (covers `root_cause_cache` and all other `otel` tables)
3. **SELECT grants**: On `otel.*`
4. **INSERT grant**: On `otel.root_cause_cache` for cache upserts (project-scoped CH user)

The policy uses `AS PERMISSIVE` on the whole database; with a single policy per user, effective access is still rows where `ProjectId` matches that project. (Other policies on the same user combine per ClickHouse permissive/restrictive rules.)

**Cluster support**: For clustered ClickHouse deployments (production), set `CLICKHOUSE_CLUSTER_NAME=pulse-clickhouse`. All DDL statements (`CREATE USER`, `CREATE ROW POLICY`, `GRANT`, `DROP`, `ALTER`) will include `ON CLUSTER` to replicate across all shards/replicas.

For local CLI queries, use the admin credentials from `deploy/.env`:
- User: `OTEL_CLICKHOUSE_USER` (default: `pulse_user`)
- Password: `OTEL_CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD` (default: `pulse_password`)

## Schema Conventions

- **Project column name**: New `otel` tables must declare the project key as exactly **`ProjectId`** (PascalCase). CI rejects other spellings that normalize to the same intent (`project_id`, `projectId`, `proj_id`, `PROJECT_ID`, etc.) via [`.github/scripts/lint_otel_clickhouse_project_column.py`](.github/scripts/lint_otel_clickhouse_project_column.py). Legacy exception: `project_monthly_usage` uses `project_id` until migrated.
- Use `MergeTree` engine with `ORDER BY` tuples for efficient range queries
- Partition by date (or `(ProjectId, date)` in replicated setup) for time-series data
- `DateTime64(9)` for nanosecond timestamps
- Map columns for flexible attributes
- `LowCardinality(String)` for low-cardinality materialized columns

## Query Rules

- Always include a time-range filter on the time column (`Timestamp` on traces/logs/stack traces and on the `otel_metrics` view; `TimeUnix` on physical OTLP metric tables)
- Use `LIMIT` on all queries
- Prefer `toDateTime64()` for timestamp comparisons
- Use materialized columns (e.g., `Platform`, `AppVersion`) over Map access
- Use the project-scoped ClickHouse user for app queries to enforce `ProjectId` isolation
